  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 133 AM EDT Mon Oct 26 2026\n\nCurrently, ridging is centered just to our west with surface high \npressure across the eastern U.S. This pattern will continue \nsubsidence and promote a cool morning today, followed by mild \ndaytime highs in the 70s. Efficient mixing will allow for RH values \nto drop into the 30s area-wide, but thankfully a weak MSLP gradient \nwill keep winds very light. By Tuesday, the ridge will move over the \nregion, causing height rises and temperatures rising further into \nthe 70s. With even more efficient mixing, lower RH values into the \n20s are likely for some. The pattern will be similar again on \nWednesday with some suppression of the ridge to our east, leading to \na very slight drop in daytime highs. By Thursday, the flow will \nbecome more zonal aloft with similarly mild daytime highs expected. \n\nBy Friday, a shortwave will eject out of the Rockies with additional \nridging expected over our region downstream. Surface high pressure \nand will keep conditions similar to previous days. For Halloween, \nthe ridge will push off to our east as the shortwave approaches from \nthe west. Depending on moisture advection and evolution of the \nshortwave, rain chances will return but currently look to be more \ntowards Sunday or later.",
